+
+# Long-rental 10% discount
+
+## Request
+
+We want to reward customers who stay longer. A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full
+price. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## School rules (requirements)
+
+- R1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+- R3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day
+  after the last rented day.
+- D1. A rental of 3 or more whole days gets 10% off its full price (`dailyPrice * days`). A rental of 1 or
+  2 days costs its full price.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1. `quote` returns the full price for a rental of 1 or 2 days, unchanged from task-001 AC2. (D1, R3)
+- AC2. `quote` returns the full price less 10% for a rental of 3 or more days, an integer in euro cents.
+  The discount is applied to the whole rental, not per day. Exactly 3 days qualifies. (D1, R1)
+- AC3. Where the 10% leaves a fraction of a cent, the total is rounded to the nearest cent, halves rounding
+  up. (R1)
+- AC4. `book` returns the same discounted total as `quote` for the same period. (D1)
+- AC5. The discount does not change the availability rules, and `quote` still does not check availability.
+  (task-001 AC7, AC8)
+- AC6. Errors for unknown items and invalid periods are unchanged. (task-001 AC5, AC6)
+
+Supersedes task-001 AC2 for rentals of 3 or more days only: those are priced at 90% of `dailyPrice * days`.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Test first (red, then green). Each acceptance criterion has at least one happy-path test and one
+error-path or edge-path test. Tests cover the boundary at 2 and 3 days, a rounding case, and that `book`
+and `quote` agree. Tests are deterministic: no wall-clock time, no randomness, no external services.
+
+Existing test `several days cost the daily price times the number of days` (3 days, sail at 1800) asserts
+the old full price for a 3-day rental; it is updated to the discounted total as part of this change.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Discounts for other durations, and any other pricing rule.
+- Cancellations and refunds.
+- Persistence across restarts.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Tests first: 5 new tests in `tests/rental.test.ts` (quote: two-day full price, three-day discount, a
+  seven-day rental, rounding; book: discounted booking total, booking total equals quote), and the old
+  3-day assertion updated. Red before the change: 5 failing, 36 passing.
+- Implementation: `src/index.ts` applies the discount in `priced`, the helper both `quote` and `book` use,
+  so the two totals cannot drift apart. `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS = 3`.
+- Result: `npm test` passes, 41 of 41 (36 existing and 5 new). Type-checking with `tsc` was not run: no
+  TypeScript compiler is installed in this repository.
+- Choices made: the discount is `Math.round(dailyPrice * days * 9 / 10)`, so a half cent rounds up and the
+  arithmetic stays in integers; the 10% is applied to the whole rental, not per day; exactly 3 days qualifies.
